<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:49:18 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>First Youth Olympic Games in Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa</link><description>
In tonight's show, the Senegalese capital is hosting the first Olympic event ever held in Africa, welcoming nearly 2,700 athletes for the 2026 Youth Olympic Games. Also, South Africa’s local elections are set for November 4, with the African National Congress facing growing pressure over its record in local government. And finally we are joined by Muse L'Artiste who's reconnecting to her roots with her latest EP Heritage bringing her father's compositions back to life.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9239705c-d4a9-11f1-aacb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9e60a5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9239705c-d4a9-11f1-aacb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9e60a5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca5497e8-d4a7-11f1-ae3f-a1a5294fe4d4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:48:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers</link><description>
While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3f32cba-d44b-11f1-873d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-dc16521b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d93e6f8a-d444-11f1-aaf8-15429d64cfb0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:06:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 60 Christians killed in Ethiopia amid rising religious violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence</link><description>
At least 60 Christians have been killed in Ethiopia in what the Orthodox Church has declared as religious violence. It is still unclear who was behind the attack, with rebels and local government blaming each other. Around 20 houses have been burned down, as FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b965392-d44c-11f1-9c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-46bebd36.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d327128a-d446-11f1-94a8-c5ddd4874f79</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal gears up for historic 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Dakar</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar</link><description>
The International Olympic Committee is upbeat just 24 hours before competition gets under way at the 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Senegal. Venues are ready to host the first-ever Olympic event on the African continent. FRANCE 24's correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b53b7c32-d44d-11f1-ada0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6cca01f2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31bfe5a2-d44b-11f1-aad5-6df4798b8782</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tanzania: 2025 election violence still traumatises, one year on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on</link><description>
Tanzania is marking the first anniversary of a bloody election that left many traumatised. The October 29, 2025 election, in which President Samia Suluhu Hassan won with 98 percent of the vote after most of the opposition was excluded, triggered days of protests that security forces brutally suppressed. Many government critics say they still fear abduction, arbitrary arrest and politically motivated prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cfc6408-d44e-11f1-b7a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5fb1d914.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb5f5748-d44b-11f1-822e-7fb8cd2f846a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:55:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Tunisians drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-in-ukraine</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Concern is growing in Tunisia as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for an answer about the fate of their loved ones forcibly conscripted to the war in Ukraine. Also, a year after Tanzania's controversial election, fear hasn't faded. And Dakar is ready to make history, as the first Olympic event ever held on African soil gets underway this weekend. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e3b7f9e-d453-11f1-b60c-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0a159d9a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e3b7f9e-d453-11f1-b60c-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0a159d9a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">598bbdc8-d3e1-11f1-b9a1-ffdbf081a42b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:48:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Across Africa: Real estate scams on the rise in Ivory Coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-real-estate-scams-growing-in-ivory-coast</link><description>
This week in Across Africa: In Ivory Coast, a severe housing shortage has fuelled demand for land, creating opportunities for fraudsters selling fake properties and non-existent plots. Also, Kenya's women are changing the game. From the track to the boxing ring, female athletes are delivering some of the country’s biggest sporting successes. Plus Addis Ababa pushes ahead with ambitious plans to become East Africa's clean-energy powerhouse.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd846a12-d470-11f1-ad0f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-334a8094.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd846a12-d470-11f1-ad0f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-334a8094.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e72d9274-d3ae-11f1-894b-f5d04db9dbe9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:43:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo: A centre celebrates the discharge of last Ebola patients</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-dr-congo-a-centre-celebrates-the-discharge-of-last-ebola-patients</link><description>
Medical staff and residents at a treatment centre in Ituri danced and sang to celebrate a first since May: the centre is no longer treating any confirmed Ebola cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aed2a692-d3ba-11f1-b307-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-RDC-Ebola-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aed2a692-d3ba-11f1-b307-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-RDC-Ebola-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf178a9e-d3ba-11f1-8363-1bb562418fc6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:13:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Putin seeks to expand ties with African countries at Russia-Africa summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday hosted dozens of African leaders at a Russia-Africa summit, part of Moscow’s efforts to expand its influence across the continent. The Russia-Africa summit marks a renewed Kremlin effort to bolster ties with a continent of nearly 1.6 billion people that is increasingly assertive on the global stage. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c0aa0bc-d37f-11f1-bedb-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T091823Z-1533690092-RC2WCOA2IVT4-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-AFRICA-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c0aa0bc-d37f-11f1-bedb-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-29T091823Z-1533690092-RC2WCOA2IVT4-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-AFRICA-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9182ffe-d37b-11f1-a580-6f50dc8232ce</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:32:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DRC: C64 opposition coalition meets in Rome, calls for inclusive dialogue</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue</link><description>
Democratic Republic ⁠of Congo's main ​opposition coalition, C64, met in Rome on Tuesday. Under pressure to respond to Joseph Kabila’s rebellion, its five leaders addressed the situation in the country from the Italian capital. They condemned any seizure of power by force and called for inclusive dialogue. FRANCE 24’s Emmet Livingston reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e046638-d380-11f1-9913-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-aad464c0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e046638-d380-11f1-9913-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-aad464c0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eea3f77c-d37d-11f1-9a48-a7be7c903c4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:28:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger: Guards accused of 'cruel, inhuman' treatment after 33 die in detention</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention</link><description>
In Niger, guards ignored the panicked cries for help from 33 detainees who died in a detention cell last month. Reports indicate that 72 people were crowded into a poorly ventilated, 20-square-metre space, where dozens slowly suffocated over 11 hours. The cell may have been cleaned and disinfected before it could be investigated. FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya has more.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57aff1c4-d38a-11f1-9cd7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-99a1b234.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57aff1c4-d38a-11f1-9cd7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-99a1b234.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82b2af6a-d385-11f1-8861-bb5448debf37</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:17:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya's female athletes make their mark as Youth Olympic Games approach</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach</link><description>
Senegal is preparing to host the Youth Olympic Games, which begin this weekend. The young athletes who hope to showcase their talents on the international stage have their sights set on the Games, and Kenya has made sure that its young boxers remain on their toes and are ready to take on opponents of a higher calibre. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f5e0bd6-d381-11f1-9ace-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f8d19214.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9f5e0bd6-d381-11f1-9ace-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f8d19214.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27406a60-d37f-11f1-9cc5-5550795cf039</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:45:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Somalia: Lower house of parliament passes bill on sexual violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence</link><description>
The Somali Parliament has passed a new law against sexual violence. The country’s criminal code dated back to 1962 and had not been updated since. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil met with Sofia Rajab in Nairobi. She is the program manager at the NGO Legal Action Worldwide, an organisation that lobbied Somali authorities in support of this new law.
 

 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc348a58-d37e-11f1-986c-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-215145-215503-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc348a58-d37e-11f1-986c-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-215145-215503-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c13f2a9e-d37e-11f1-aad7-0575b2c8fa36</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:42:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Russia woos African leaders at Moscow summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-woos-african-leaders-at-moscow-summit</link><description>
In tonight's edition: A summit with nearly two dozen African leaders opens in Moscow, with the Kremlin describing their countries as natural allies against the West. Also, Nigerian investigators say that dozens of detained miners who died in a crowded jail cell screamed for help as jailors ignored their suffering. And ahead of the Youth Olympics in Senegal, Kenya is ramping up support for its female athletes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3402d47c-d316-11f1-961e-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-866022cb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3402d47c-d316-11f1-961e-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-866022cb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad00f5e4-d315-11f1-84d6-0b9f1f6718eb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:27:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Putin woos African leaders as Moscow seeks to expand footprint in Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-putin-woos-african-leaders-moscow-seeks-expand-footprint-africa</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin sought to woo African leaders and government delegates on Wednesday as they gathered in Moscow for the third Russia-Africa Summit to discuss trade, security, arms deals and grain supplies as part of the Kremlin's strategic efforts to expand its footprint in Africa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6edccb5c-d2f8-11f1-8803-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4NG2RM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6edccb5c-d2f8-11f1-8803-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4NG2RM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7985588-d2f5-11f1-9638-895e8d570f68</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:13:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6edccb5c-d2f8-11f1-8803-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4NG2RM.jpg">© Igor Ivanko, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ethiopia clashes push 50,000 to flee to Kenya</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-ethiopia-clashes-push-50-000-flee-to-kenya</link><description>
The outbreak of fighting between rival forces in southern Ethiopia last week has led some 50,000 people to seek refuge in neighbouring Kenya, the United Nations said Wednesday, citing local authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d010580-c3eb-11f1-bc45-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QU7ZZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d010580-c3eb-11f1-bc45-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QU7ZZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">116ff416-d2e5-11f1-bbc3-a3917e46df4e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:29:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d010580-c3eb-11f1-bc45-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2QU7ZZ.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Africa's Ebola outbreak tops 10,000 cases, mainly in DR Congo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261027-africa-ebola-outbreak-tops-10-000-cases-mainly-dr-congo</link><description>
Africa's outbreak of the Ebola virus has passed more than 10,000 cases, health authorities said Tuesday, with the vast majority located in Democratic Republic of Congo. There are currently no approved vaccines for the rare Bundibugyo species of Ebola driving the current infections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea553966-d219-11f1-a266-f94f8c9bba93</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:45:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg">© Sebastien Kitsa Musayi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sudan: One year after the fall of El-Fasher</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher</link><description>
It has been one year since the fall of El-Fasher in Sudan, a city in North Darfur, which was captured by the Rapid Support Forces. At least 6,000 civilians were killed by rebel troops as they entered this strategic city.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/406be9ce-d1ea-11f1-b8bf-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-214358-214533-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/406be9ce-d1ea-11f1-b8bf-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-214358-214533-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46063f9c-d1ea-11f1-80ae-350239596e70</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:46:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications after recent unrest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest</link><description>
Tensions in South Africa over anti-migrant protests have left in limbo many who were counting on following the rules to sort out their paperwork and status in the country. Calls for a crackdown on foreigners, particularly undocumented migrants, have sometimes spiralled into murder. In response to the unrest, the government suspended the asylum application process.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e080c762-d1f0-11f1-a0e1-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3a9aa983.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e080c762-d1f0-11f1-a0e1-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3a9aa983.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da3c8bea-d1ee-11f1-a77e-13226d517053</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:37:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Algeria to deploy army units to Niger to protect economic interests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests</link><description>
Algeria will send army units to Niger to ​protect energy and economic interests, according to a statement from the presidency on Monday (October 26). Algeria's Parliament held an emergency vote on Sunday on what would be Algeria's first such foreign mission since 1973.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddd4cfa-d1f0-11f1-98ed-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1bc55d9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddd4cfa-d1f0-11f1-98ed-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1bc55d9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ce0aefa-d1ed-11f1-8f3f-3f3d8cf5602f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:28:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chad hosts hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees as regional humanitarian crisis extends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-extends</link><description>
Sudan’s war is spilling over into Chad. A drone strike killed at least four people last week in the border town of Bamina, and hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees have crossed over in search of safety. Many of those who survived the massacre in El Fasher are still deeply traumatised. FRANCE 24's correspondent Harold Girard has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b861376e-d1ee-11f1-b904-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4e39aeb0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b861376e-d1ee-11f1-b904-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4e39aeb0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">149bffd0-d1ec-11f1-bdfd-7d7dd1394a0b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:13:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>The fall of Sudan's El-Fasher, one year on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on</link><description>
In tonight's edition: 15 military officials in Sudan are sanctioned by the UK over the brutality and abuse of civilians during the fall of El-Fasher. Also, ⁠Algeria is set to send in army units ​to ‌Niger ⁠to ‌protect energy ⁠and economic interests there. And days after a foreigner was beaten to death on the streets of Durban, the stalled asylum process has left many migrants in South Africa living in fear. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97719272-d1eb-11f1-ae97-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e8379615.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97719272-d1eb-11f1-ae97-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e8379615.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80957748-d183-11f1-9ec6-a3934f97f5ba</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:26:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Algeria to send troops to Niger in first foreign deployment in over 50 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years</link><description>
Algeria’s parliament on Sunday approved a resolution to send troops to Niger, making the first time Algerian soldiers will be deployed abroad since the 1973 Arab-Israeli war. Niger faces persistent attacks by armed groups, including near its border with Algeria, and the deployment comes as Algiers and Niamey are building the Trans-Saharan Gas Pipeline after decades of delays. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f578d036-d120-11f1-b522-ff2dd1b862e1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:10:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg">© Fateh Guidoum, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Building collapse in Nairobi: Search for survivors under way</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Rescuers comb through rubble in a bid to reach trapped survivors after a multi-storey building under construction in Nairobi collapses. Also, Kenya announces a second Ebola death. Earlier this week it had logged nine cases, all traced back to its first Ebola patient who died earlier this month. Finally, with the 11th edition of the iconic contemporary art festival Also Known as Africa taking place in Paris, we speak to Cape Verdean artist Amadeo Carvalho.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ca47780-cf20-11f1-a61d-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bed663fa.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ca47780-cf20-11f1-a61d-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bed663fa.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1750ef52-cf20-11f1-996d-211c1872ac14</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:31:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>SA faces rising tension as foreign national is killed amid anti-migrant protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests</link><description>
South African police are investigating the murder of a foreign national after violent protests by anti-immigrant groups swept through the central business district in Durban. The latest death follows months of violent rallies in which at least 10 foreigners were killed and several other countries on the continent raced to repatriate their people. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d03acde-cec3-11f1-9b9e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-214526-214702-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d03acde-cec3-11f1-9b9e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-214526-214702-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">828bb12e-cec3-11f1-8b0b-9b797395f52e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:08:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Across Africa: Ivorian vinyl head's heritage hunt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt</link><description>
This week in Across Africa: Ivorian music lover Cédric Kouamé is on a mission to restore 20th-century African vinyl and bring old-school sounds back to modern playlists. Also, 10 years after Cameroon's worst railway disaster, families are still fighting for justice for the 79 people killed. Finally, in São Tomé and Príncipe, we discover how the islands' rich volcanic soils produce some of the world's most distinctive vanilla.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8dd2770-cecb-11f1-9d94-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-000d2b86.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8dd2770-cecb-11f1-9d94-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-000d2b86.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">771742aa-ce5e-11f1-9758-156ff0704180</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:27:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Olympic fever grips Senegal as Dakar hosts Youth Olympic Games</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog</link><description>
As Senegal prepares to host the Youth Olympic Games (YOG), the first Olympic event ever organised in Africa, the country is pulling out all the stops to be ready on time. FRANCE 24’s Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/239dc254-ce1b-11f1-a7da-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-EN-reporters.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/239dc254-ce1b-11f1-a7da-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-EN-reporters.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf59236a-ce1e-11f1-ad2c-6796427f56e6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Simon MARTIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ivory Coast: Children face serious health risks from lead in paint</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint</link><description><![CDATA[
Across Ivory Coast, teams are going door-to-door, testing homes for dangerous levels of lead as efforts to raise awareness of the toxic metal’s health risks intensify. Report by Jean Barrère & Guillaume Gougeon.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc97410-ceba-11f1-a099-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082335-082547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc97410-ceba-11f1-a099-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082335-082547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c22a6afe-ceba-11f1-90f8-7fb21b4796f0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:37:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Africa faces 'complex' Ebola outbreak after spread to Nigeria: WHO</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who</link><description>
The World Health Organization warned Thursday that Africa faced a "complex" Ebola outbreak after the virus crossed from east Africa to Nigeria, marking the first case in the west of the continent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7e9f0b4-ceba-11f1-9d55-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082125-082315-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7e9f0b4-ceba-11f1-9d55-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082125-082315-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bcae43ca-ceba-11f1-9e94-1f871d4d611b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africa gripped by anti-migrant protests as foreign national is killed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed</link><description>
Xenophobic unrest turns deadly in South Africa as a foreign national is beaten to death during a protest march in Durban, a city increasingly gripped by anti-migrant tensions. Meanwhile, as global efforts to raise awareness of lead poisoning intensify, teams in Ivory Coast go door-to-door testing homes for dangerous levels of the toxic metal. Finally, Ivorian authorities are cracking down on illegal mining over fears of pollution, but some young people say the activity remains one of their few sources of income. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49e20596-ceb7-11f1-b7ca-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-78054085.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49e20596-ceb7-11f1-b7ca-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-78054085.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8400964-ce65-11f1-b3cc-f319924fdc6e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:24:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
